   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to authorizing the dormitory authority to finance stand-alone clinical facilities for various human services organizations for whom the dormitory authority is currently authorized to issue bonds and notes",
    "basePrintNo": "S5294",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5294-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5294\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to authorizing the dormitory authority to finance stand-alone\nclinical facilities for various human services organizations for whom\nthe dormitory authority is currently authorized to issue bonds and\nnotes\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe bill would authorize the Dormitory Authority (\"DASNY\") to finance\nstand-alone clinical facilities for certain human services\norganizations for whom DASNY is currently authorized to issue bonds\nand notes.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend Public Authorities Law §§\n1676(2)(b) and 1680(1) to extend DASNY's authorization to provide\nfinancing and other services on behalf of NYSARC, Inc., Alliance of\nLong Island Agencies, Inc., and not-for-profit members of the\nInteragency Council of Mental Retardation and Developmental\nDisabilities Agencies, Inc., to each entity's clinical facilities.\n\nSection 2 of this bill would set forth the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDASNY is currently authorized to finance clinical facilities, in\naddition to educational, administrative, residential and day\nprogramming facilities, on behalf of the New York State Rehabilitation\nAssociation and United Cerebral Palsy Association affiliates. This\nbill would align DASNY's authorization on behalf of NYSARC, Inc., IAC\nand the Alliance with DASNY's authorization with these other service\nproviders. Authorizing DASNY to provide additional sources of\nfinancing to assist these entities develop clinic facilities will\nenhance the provision of essential healthcare services by such\norganizations and promote the State's Delivery System Reform Incentive\nPayment (DSRIP) program, the purpose of which is to reform the State's\nhealth care system and reduce costs.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
